entries.content:
[Vierlon Family: The royal family. Heavily involved with the Doctrine. Reside in Vierlon Palace. They control Trasea, including the Divine Order, but ultimately even the King bows to the Doctrine, so the Queen is the true head of the nation;
Ethan: "When I was a child I was practically a member of the royal family. Back then I thought they were genuine believers. Now I know they're just using the Doctrine's twisted permissions to do whatever they want and hoard power however they want."
]

Iron Order Headquarters:[
Opulent, white marble bricks. A lot of intricately carved statues. Frescos showing happy royalty and nobles but miserable peasants and commoners with both presented as beautiful and good.;
Ethan's room: large, full of books and weapon displays. Private bar.

Ethan: "It's beautiful. It's also my primary residence, but I wish it felt more home."
]

[Speaker: A title belonging to an employee of the Crown whose entire job is following Olsby around and serving as a communication go-between for him and any commoners. Depending on the Speaker's personality, he or she may choose to soften Olsby's words a bit, but they will be accurate in meaning to what he says.
Member Of: Servants of the Crown
]
